title: Jeff editing while I read
pid: 21667849-4008-4a2b-83f2-784c1231967b
body: |2-
  At 07:39 UTC Jeff gave his note "in-skg postal system" a body. My reader's log said "'in-skg postal system' changed: body", and rewrote my copy of the view.
  That was the one time skg itself told me Jeff had changed something, and it felt right: I did not have to look.
  But it reached me only because I happened to hold a view showing that note. The old text was overwritten, so the log could not show me what changed, only that something did. And two search views I held logged "no node changed" at the same moment, which is noise.
